What are Grafana Alerts?

Grafana Alerting allows you to create alerts from:

Prometheus metrics
Loki logs
Elasticsearch
InfluxDB
MySQL/Postgres
CloudWatch
Azure Monitor
Many other data sources

Unlike Prometheus alerts, Grafana can combine multiple data sources into one alert.



Architecture:

                Prometheus
                     |
             Stores Metrics
                     |
              +--------------+
              |   Grafana    |
              |--------------|
              | Dashboards   |
              | Alert Rules  |
              | Contact Pts  |
              | Notification |
              +--------------+
                     |
             Email / Slack / Teams

Grafana Alerting Components

There are four main components.

1. Alert Rule

Defines WHEN an alert should fire.

Example:

CPU > 80%

or

prediction_requests_total == 0


2. Contact Point

Defines WHERE to send notifications.

Examples:

Email
Slack
Microsoft Teams
Telegram
PagerDuty
Discord


3. Notification Policy

Defines WHICH alerts go to WHICH contact point.

Example

Critical
        |
        v
     Email + Slack

Warning
        |
        v
       Email

4. Silences

Temporarily suppress alerts.

Example

Sunday Maintenance

No alerts
2 PM - 4 PM


